# Diagnostics

**Status:** current. Rocci does not yet publish a stable diagnostic ID catalog
for the template language. Do not invent codes in prose. Rocdown catalog codes
(`RD2101`, …) belong to [Rocdown](/docs/rocdown/).

Organize failures by **owning phase** and the **exact leading message**.

| Phase | Typical surface | Where to look |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Rocci parse / lower | `rocci build` / `inspect` | Template diagnostics; source maps |
| Roc compile | `roc` after lowering | Roc compiler; generated Roc |
| Application effects | `@init` / handlers | `?` → process exit or HTTP 500 |
| HTTP dispatch | wrong method/path | `--log-handlers`; handler matrix |
| Webview / preview | window does not open | `--no-window`; Linux WebKitGTK |

Until codes exist, quote the leading message in issues. Migration from
removed `@on` is a rewrite diagnostic, not a deprecation warning.

**Related:** [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting/), [Grammar](/docs/reference/language/grammar/).
